[decoded] "Based on your notes from Meeting 1, here is a structured summary and technical breakdown of the **GatedDeltaNet** architecture you described. This appears to be a hybrid approach designed to balance the efficiency of recurrent states with the expressiveness of attention mechanisms.\n\n### Architecture Overview: GatedDeltaNet\n\nThis layer replaces the standard Key-Value (KV) cache found in standard attention mechanisms with a **recurrent state mechanism** that operates per value head.\n\n#### 1. Core Mechanism\nInstead of storing static KV pairs for every position, the layer maintains a dynamic **recurrent state** ($s_t$) for each value head.\n\n*   **State Decay**: At every position $t$, the state decays by a learned factor ($\\alpha$). This prevents the state from accumulating irrelevant information over long sequences without regularization.\n    $$s_t = \\alpha \\cdot s_{t-1}$$\n*   **Prediction & Retrieval**: The"
